entityDescription:
The Cluster of Bioeconomy and Environment of Western Macedonia (CluBE) is a non-profit company established among local actors and stakeholders of the Region of Western Macedonia in Greece. CluBE emerged since early &rsquo;00s from the continuous collaboration of regional players during previous projects, analysing regional bioenergy and biomass potentials, the core cluster structures, and the regional innovation systems devoted to the energy sector.
The mission of CluBE is to enhance collaboration and increase regional knowledge by promoting innovation and synergies between regional stakeholders in the fields of bioeconomy and environment.
The Region of Western Macedonia has a population of 255.056, and covers a total surface of 9.451 km2 (7,2% of the country&rsquo;s total). The nature of the region is mountainous, with Aliakmonas river crossing through the entire Region. Western Macedonia is situated in the northern part of Greece and borders with Albania and North Macedonia. It is the only region without sea coast. Western Macedonia is divided into the regional units of Kozani, Grevena, Kastoria and Florina. The productive character of the Region is determined primarily by the energy industry and secondarily by the fur industry. Other important economic activities in the area, which is gaining importance in the current transition phase, are the agrifood sector and the marble mining.
CluBE is developing R&D and business activities in the fields of bioeconomy, bioenergy and environment, in order to reinforce green, smart and circular economy in the region and the neighbouring areas, namely through:&bull;
Energetic exploitation of biomass for household and industrial use, and especially for district heating systems for small, medium or large cities.&bull;
Mobilisation of regional biomass supply chains.&bull;
Development of the green hydrogen economy.&bull;
Increase of the share of biofuels in the energy mix of transportation fuels.&bull;
Co-firing biomass with lignite in existing power stations and/or future heating plants.&bull;
Optimisation of heating systems.&bull;
Improvement of energy efficiency for households, public and private buildings.&bull;
Promote the concepts of smart cities and villages.&bull;
Support of the entrepreneurship in the field of circular bioeconomy.

